OL,3,AAt least seven months of relentless
OL,4,Arain needed to end drought, research
OL,5,Ashows
OL,6,
OL,7,FAbove-average rainfall is needed across
OL,8,FEngland for the next seven months for
OL,9,Fall areas to recover from drought by
OL,10,Fspring 2027, according to new research.
OL,12,FThe Environment Agency (EA) stated that
OL,13,Fdespite some wet weather during the
OL,14,Ffirst half of September, almost
OL,15,Fthree-quarters of England remains in
OL,16,Fdrought following an exceptionally dry
OL,17,Fspring and summer as well as a
OL,18,Fsuccession of heatwaves.
OL,20,FIt says around 120% of typical rainfall
OL,21,Fis needed between now and April for all
OL,22,Fareas to be considered out of drought.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/38
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,0,100
